hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1606","Narrated to us Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi, who said: narrated to us Khalid ibn al-Harith. And it was also narrated to us by Bundar, who said: narrated to us 'Uthman—meaning ibn 'Umar—who both said: narrated to us Ibn Abi Dhi'b—this is the hadith of Khalid ibn al-Harith—on the authority of his maternal uncle, al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Salim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, on the authority of his father ['Abd Allah ibn 'Umar] (RA), who said:\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would command us to recite lightly and would lead us in prayer with Surah as-Saffat.\""\n\n---\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"1607","Narrated to us Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzar: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri informed us; ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-‘Abbas narrated to us, from ‘Ammar al-Duhni, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said:\n\My father had abandoned praying with us. I asked him"," 'Why do you not pray with us?' He replied"," 'Because you shorten the prayer.' I said"," 'Where then is the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Indeed"," among you are the weak"," the elderly"," and those with needs\""?' He said"," 'I heard ‘Abd Allah ibn Mas‘ud say that.' Then he prayed with us three times what you pray in one.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
